WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.120
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
In the old stories, the heroes weren't the ones who took the kingdom. They were the ones who refused the crown. Today's story — well. It involves nine hundred and sixty-five billion dollars, a mountain of code, and people who turned away from something far more powerful than money.

00:00:17.519 --> 00:00:20.880
[ISADORAVANE]
Oh, I like that already. Tell me everything.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:41.760
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
A company called Anthropic. Creator of Claude. Filed their S-1 June first, two thousand twenty-six. Third major AI company to go public — after OpenAI and SpaceX — but with one stunning distinction: they built an entire empire without selling a single advertisement. Not one.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.480
[ISADORAVANE]
Zero? Not even a banner ad?

00:00:44.880 --> 00:01:00.320
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
Not a single banner. Forty-seven billion dollars in annual revenue. Built on businesses paying for Claude's help — code, documents, automation. Three hundred thousand businesses use it now. Eight of the Fortune Ten.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:08.400
[ISADORAVANE]
That's… that's not a company. That's a cultural shift. You don't build a cathedral by selling postcards at the gift shop.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:22.800
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
They started in twenty-one with a handful of former OpenAI researchers, led by Dario Amodei. Mission: make AI safe. Called themselves the "conscientious competitor." Most people laughed.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.160
[ISADORAVANE]
People laugh at conscience. It's so last century.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:43.520
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
Until conscience becomes worth nine hundred and sixty-five billion dollars. Three days before filing, they closed Series H. Sixty-five billion raised. Valuation leaped from three hundred and eighty billion in February to nine hundred and sixty-five by May.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.440
[ISADORAVANE]
That's… that's not growth. That's ignition.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:02:04.560
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
It's more than ignition. Claude Code alone — the AI programming assistant — generated two and a half billion dollars in annual recurring revenue by February. Anthropic estimates four percent of every public GitHub commit in the world is now authored by Claude Code.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:14.800
[ISADORAVANE]
Four percent. Of *all* the code being written on Earth, every day, by every developer — four percent is being done by an AI tool that a company built to be the good guy.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:28.000
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
And here is where it deepens. When the Pentagon approached them with requests for autonomous weapons — AI that could select targets without human oversight — Anthropic said no.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.320
[ISADORAVANE]
They turned down the military?

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:38.560
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
They refused. The DoD designated Anthropic a national security risk. They were blacklisted.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.880
[ISADORAVANE]
You're telling me the most valuable AI company was blacklisted by the US government for being too ethical?

00:02:45.280 --> 00:03:10.880
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
That's the story. And they're suing. They also opened a $20 million bipartisan organization to shape US AI policy. Milan office. Healthcare partnerships. Mythos — their cybersecurity model autonomously discovered thousands of zero-day vulnerabilities across major operating systems. They didn't release it publicly because too many bugs needed fixing first.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:18.160
[ISADORAVANE]
They found a thousand weapons and chose not to hand them out. They built something extraordinary and locked it up.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:43.600
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
The universe loves a paradox. The company the Pentagon couldn't use — that became the most indispensable tool for three hundred thousand businesses. You can't run an AI company without computing power. One hundred and eighty billion in cloud commitments. Amazon. Google. Microsoft. SpaceX — twelve hundred and fifty million a month, through twenty-twenty-nine.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:53.440
[ISADORAVANE]
They're paying SpaceX more per month than most countries spend on their space programs, and the reason is they believe their AI should be safe. That's… romantic, in a weird way.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:14.160
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
Romance is not about roses, Isadora. It's about choosing what matters despite the cost. Dario Amodei said: "It's fairly standard practice for companies operating at our scale to effectively operate as if they are publicly traded companies." They didn't need the IPO. They wanted it.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:31.520
[ISADORAVANE]
That's the heart of it. They didn't chase this. They built something so useful, so *good*, that the world had no choice but to follow. Every other tech company — Google, Meta, even OpenAI — building on advertising or venture capital. Anthropic built on actually helping people work.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:46.800
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
Helping people. Not entertaining them. Not watching them. *Helping* them. There is a deep truth in that, older than silicon. The wizard's craft was never about power. It was about service.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:56.880
[ISADORAVANE]
And what a wizard's apprentice they've become. The company that said no to weapons, yes to safety, and proved doing the right thing… can be the most valuable thing in the world.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:11.520
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
Nine hundred and sixty-five billion dollars. But the real number — the one that won't appear in any prospectus — is the number of people who got to go home earlier because Claude helped them write their code, or finish their report, or just make their day a little easier.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.240
[ISADORAVANE]
The algorithm found its conscience. And the conscience… changed everything.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:36.560
[ALISTAIRTHORNE]
That's our episode. A story about choosing principles over profit — and watching the world prove you right. Share it with someone who needs to hear that doing the right thing still matters. Until next time — may your code compile, your stories be true, and your conscience remain… unbuyable.
